write('/resources/','Underwater Inspection Guides & Downloads','Buying guides, technical guides, spec sheets and project checklists for underwater inspection ROVs, cleaning and dredging robots.',res,og_image='r-45.png')
camera=intro('TECHNICAL GUIDE / SENSING','Camera vs sonar for underwater inspection','The right comparison starts with the inspection question, not the sensor name.')
camera+='<section class="wrap section article-grid"><aside class="article-aside"><h3>Prepare these inputs</h3><ul><li>Visibility and suspended material</li><li>Target size and inspection distance</li><li>Required detection and measurement</li><li>Position and reporting references</li></ul><a class="text-link" href="/solutions/industrial-underwater-inspection/">Industrial inspection guide</a></aside><div class="article-body">'+answer_box('Use a camera when water clarity and lighting let the operator see surface detail at the working distance. Add imaging sonar when visibility is poor, to navigate and recognise structures acoustically. Many inspections combine both: sonar to find the target, the camera for close visual evidence.')+'<section><h2>What a camera contributes</h2><p>Optical video can show recognizable surface detail, markings and material appearance when light and water clarity allow. Lighting position, suspended particles, standoff distance and camera control affect what the operator can interpret.</p><p>A sharp image does not automatically provide scaled dimensions. Measurement needs an appropriate reference or calibrated method.</p></section><section><h2>What imaging sonar contributes</h2><p>Sonar uses acoustic information and can be useful for navigation and feature recognition where optical visibility is poor. Interpretation depends on the sonar type, frequency, geometry and target.</p><p>Imaging, profiling and bathymetric sonar serve different purposes. An optional sonar interface is not proof that a particular sensor or reporting workflow has been integrated.</p></section><section><h2>Why a combined package may be appropriate</h2><p>Sonar may help the operator approach or find a target; the camera may then provide local visual detail. Confirm that both data streams can be recorded, referenced and interpreted for the actual defect or condition.</p></section><section><h2>Ask for task-relevant samples</h2><p>Request footage and acoustic data from comparable visibility, geometry and target conditions. Agree what must be detected, how it will be located and what counts as acceptable evidence.</p></section></div></section>'
camera+='<section class="section band"><div class="wrap table-scroll"><table><caption>Questions for the sensing review</caption><thead><tr><th>Requirement</th><th>Optical review</th><th>Acoustic review</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Surface appearance</th><td>Visibility, lighting and usable standoff</td><td>Whether the target has a relevant acoustic signature</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Navigation</th><td>Available scene detail</td><td>Field of view, range and feature recognition</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Measurement</th><td>Scale reference or calibrated method</td><td>Sensor type, geometry and expected uncertainty</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Reporting</th><td>Video, stills and annotations</td><td>Recorded formats and location reference</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section>'+cta()
write('/resources/rov-camera-vs-sonar/','Camera vs Sonar for Underwater Inspection','When to use a camera, imaging sonar or both for ROV underwater inspection: visibility, navigation, measurement and reporting.',camera,og_image='r-45.png')
checklist=intro('PROJECT GUIDE / TUNNELS','Underwater tunnel inspection planning checklist',RESOURCES[1][2])
checklist+='<section class="wrap section article-grid"><aside class="article-aside"><h3>Use this before quotation</h3><p>Unknown values are useful to identify. Mark them as unknown rather than filling them with assumptions.</p>'+link('/assets/tunnel-project-checklist.txt','Download checklist','button secondary')+'</aside><div class="article-body">'
checkrows=[('Route & geometry',['Total intended inspection length','Cross-sections, gradient and elevation profile','Bends, transitions, constrictions and known obstructions']),('Water & operating conditions',['Depth, flow range and expected visibility','Sediment and debris conditions','Isolation, shutdown and site permit requirements']),('Access & field logistics',['Entry opening and launch/recovery area','Lifting, reel location and available power','Staffing, communications and emergency access']),('Inspection & evidence',['Defects or condition to be assessed','Coverage and sensor requirements','Position reference, data formats and acceptance criteria']),('Failure & recovery',['Response to snagging or lost communication','Retrieval equipment and contact points','Exit conditions and site owner responsibilities'])]
